# Agent Profiles

An Agent Profile is a reusable choice of Agent Client, model, reasoning effort, permissions mode, and instructions. Bots use Profiles to give a helper the right specialty; [Workflows](/docs/workflows) use the same Profiles for Agent Nodes.

## Start from a template

Open **Settings → Agent Profiles**, choose **New profile**, and select a template. Built-in templates include **Researcher**, **Copywriter**, **Architect**, **Designer**, **Coder**, and **Motion designer**. A template fills the form; you can edit every field before creating the Profile.

## Fill in the Profile

Each Profile has:

- **Name**, shown in the Dashboard;
- **Profile ID**, a permanent identifier created with the Profile;
- **Description**, which tells Bots when this specialty fits;
- **Client**, **Model**, and optional reasoning effort;
- **Use YOLO mode**, which starts new work with the Profile's permissive execution mode;
- **System prompt**, containing the helper or Workflow node's working instructions.

A Profile ID must start with a lowercase letter or digit and use only lowercase letters, digits, `.`, `_`, and `-`. Choose a stable ID such as `release-reviewer`.

## Write a useful description

The Bot reads the description when deciding whether to select a Profile. State the tasks it should receive, the result it owns, and any important boundary. For example:

> Reviews API changes against the approved contract and reports breaking behavior with file references. Read-only; does not implement fixes.

Keep detailed working rules in the system prompt. A specific description helps the Bot distinguish Profiles that use similar Clients or models.

## Let a Bot manage Profiles

The Dashboard may show a card suggesting specialist Profiles. Choose a template there, or select **Ask Bot** to discuss a useful set. You can also tell any Bot to create, update, or delete a Profile in chat. The Bot checks available templates, Clients, models, and reasoning effort choices, then reports what changed.

## Reuse a Profile in Workflows

When creating or editing a Workflow, select the Profile for each Agent Node. The node starts with that Profile's Client, model, permissions mode, and instructions, alongside the node's own task and Handoff inputs.

## Understand when edits apply

Profiles are shared by every Bot on the device. Updates apply to new helpers and Workflow nodes that have not started yet. A Session that already started keeps the Profile instructions it received at creation time. Deleting a Profile leaves existing Session history intact.

Next: [run parallel Helpers](/docs/bots/helpers) or [build a Workflow](/docs/workflows).
